      "content": "It is true that trauma can ripple through families, but your presence offers a chance to introduce new coping mechanisms before the inevitable damage occurs. Blaming yourself for potential future pain ignores the way healing often requires emotional support rather than isolation. You can actively choose to break the cycle by seeking professional help and creating your own boundaries, ensuring that the worst-case scenario never becomes your reality.",
      "source": "target",
